cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "VitaNova: a collective-level Darwinian population without collective-level selection"
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Nam Hai
    family-names: Le
    email: namlehai90@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/drnamlabs-gif/vitanova"
abstract: >-
  An agent-based model in which collectives of simulated organisms form, acquire
  an internal structure, grow and divide, with no fitness function and no rule
  referring to a collective. The divisions compound into lineages up to nineteen
  collective generations deep, across which a collective-level trait is
  transmitted, giving a Darwinian population at the collective level that arises
  without collective-level selection.
keywords:
  - evolutionary transitions in individuality
  - collective reproduction
  - Darwinian populations
  - self-organisation
  - artificial life
  - agent-based model
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Emergent Collective Reproduction via Evolving Neuronal Flocks"
    authors:
      - given-names: Nam Hai
        family-names: Le
    year: 2025
